    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "So I was working on this, and I started off with `interpolated_inverted_cdf`. \r\nI added the basic indices math needed and it passed most the tests, but I keep getting `nan location mismatch error` for 2 of the test cases.\r\n```\r\nFAILED tests/cupy_tests/statistics_tests/test_order.py::TestQuantileMethods::test_quantile_out[interpolated_inverted_cdf]\r\nFAILED tests/cupy_tests/statistics_tests/test_order.py::TestQuantileMethods::test_quantile_overwrite[interpolated_inverted_cdf]\r\n```\r\n```\r\nE       AssertionError: \r\nE       Not equal to tolerance rtol=1e-06, atol=0\r\nE       \r\nE       x and y nan location mismatch:\r\nE        x: array([[[[5.650563, 5.505339, 4.453514],\r\nE                [4.81928 , 4.400868, 5.545542]],\r\nE       ...\r\nE        y: array([[[[5.650563, 5.505339, 4.453514],\r\nE                [4.81928 , 4.400868, 5.545542]],\r\nE       ...\r\n\r\ncupy\\testing\\_array.py:24: AssertionError\r\n```\r\n\r\nCould you help me by pointing out where I could be wrong?\r\n```\r\n elif method == 'interpolated_inverted_cdf':\r\n        indices = q * (Nx) - 1\r\n```",
